From 91670c12ea929db911a5a0c33884f9af31bdf57c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 03:33:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(pilot): serve the tester leg its own tester profile, not
 the executor's (GH-360)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The pilot's `tester` role maps to the `implement` session actor (it runs the
unit's tests in the executor's worktree), but `openSession` had no role axis,
so `OPEN_IMPLEMENT_SESSION` + headless ALWAYS built the executor SDK profile
("execute the approved plan ... commit the work"). The testing leg therefore
re-implemented the unit off the draft plan, reported "done", and the pilot
looped executing→checking→testing until the retreat budget was spent —
legCount 10 with 9 spawn@implement legs and 0 reviewer/author legs, abandoned (#360).

- runtime_profiles: add `buildWorkUnitClaudeTestSdkRuntimeProfile` — a
  headless TESTER profile (`PRX_AGENT_ROLE=tester`; allowlist is exactly
  Read/Grep/Glob + `Bash(bun test:*)` + `Bash(bun run:*)` +
  `Bash(prx tools git:*)`; Edit/Write denied; `omitOwnNamespace` so the tester
  does NOT inherit `Bash(prx implement:*)` and cannot re-launch the executor)
  whose prompt consumes the COMMITTED implementation and treats the plan as
  context only.
- session-entry: `OPEN_IMPLEMENT_SESSION` gains `role?: "executor"|"tester"`;
  headless + tester selects the tester profile, everything else is unchanged.
- session/schema + open: `SessionOpenInput.role` threads through to the event
  and the spawn attestation is minted at `<unit>:spawn@tester` instead of
  overwriting the executor's `spawn@implement`.
- pilot-real: `roleSessionRole` carries the tester's identity into
  `openSession` for the tester leg (same `implement` worktree, own profile).
- tests: pilot-real asserts the tester leg opens with role "tester" and runs
  the tester profile; session_entry / open / runtime_profiles cover the new
  event axis, the spawn slot, and the profile shape.

Closes #360

